---
import PortalLayout from '../layouts/PortalLayout.astro';
---

<PortalLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="How Terra Chartarum handles analytics, cookies, personal information, and external collection links."
>
  <section class="shell prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
    <h1>Read without a profile</h1>
    <p>
      Terra Chartarum is a static publication. It has no reader accounts, comments, advertising
      pixels, behavioural profiles, or forms that collect personal information.
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      Analytics is disabled unless the production build is explicitly configured with a
      site-specific Plausible Analytics script. When enabled, the integration sends aggregate
      pageviews only. Optional outbound-link, file-download, form, custom-property, hash-route and
      localhost measurements are disabled in the site code.
    </p>
    <p>
      Plausible states that its service does not use cookies or persistent identifiers, does not
      collect personal data, and processes visitor data in the European Union. See Plausible's
      <a href="https://plausible.io/privacy-focused-web-analytics">privacy overview</a>,
      <a href="https://plausible.io/privacy">privacy policy</a>, and
      <a href="https://plausible.io/compliance">compliance documentation</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      On that selected configuration, this site does not display an analytics cookie-consent banner
      because it does not set analytics cookies. If the provider, measurements, storage, or legal
      context changes, analytics must be held until this notice and the consent decision are
      reviewed again.
    </p>

    <h2>External links and media</h2>
    <p>
      Essays link to libraries, archives, map collections, scholarship, and source records.
      Following an external link takes you to another organisation with its own privacy practices.
      The portal's production images and fonts are served from the site itself; a catalogue record
      may preserve an external source URL for attribution without loading it automatically.
    </p>

    <h2>Operational logs</h2>
    <p>
      The hosting provider may process ordinary request and security logs needed to deliver and
      protect the site. Those platform logs are separate from the optional Plausible integration
      described above.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      Analytics remains a reversible feature. Removing the three public build variables removes the
      script from every generated page. Material changes to collection or tracking require an
      updated privacy review before release.
    </p>
  </section>
</PortalLayout>

<style>
  .prose {
    max-width: 72ch;
    padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem);
  }
  .prose h1 {
    margin: 0.3rem 0 1.25rem;
    font-size: var(--step-4);
  }
  .prose h2 {
    margin: 2.5rem 0 1rem;
    font-size: var(--step-2);
  }
</style>
